  "courseName": "General Physics I (Mechanics)",
  "estimatedLength": "50 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Represent a two-dimensional vector by its magnitude/direction and equivalently by its horizontal and vertical components.",
    "Add two or more vectors graphically using the tip-to-tail method and identify the resultant.",
    "Decompose a vector into components along chosen axes using right-triangle trigonometry, and reconstruct the vector from its components.",
    "Explain why horizontal and vertical motions of a projectile are independent, given that gravity acts only vertically.",
    "Describe how horizontal velocity, vertical velocity, and position of a projectile change over flight, and identify maximum height as the point of zero vertical velocity.",
    "Predict how launch angle and speed affect trajectory, range, and maximum height, and identify the angle of maximum range for a given speed."
